 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Sure. A quick plan first, then we can make it real. Zigzagging helps when you' short of time. Pick two or three big things to finish. Then give each task a couple of good chunks of time, not little bits. If you keep stopping and starting, it takes longer. Set aside a dedicated time for emails in the middle, rather than at the end. It feels much quicker if you focus on one thing at a time. Take it in small chunks. Check them every half hour or so, but try to focus on one task at a time.",
